      "message": "Flagging this \"DFP when N/C\" setting is causing issues for \"UFP capable\" devices using TCPMv1, such as ServoV4p1.\n\nServoV4p1 is a FOSS debug tool that acts as a \"DRD\u003d1 DTP\u003d1 CommCap\u003d1\" device in both directions. USB3 as UFP, USB2 as DFP. If forcefully configured into \"DFP\" role on disconnect, rather than proper \"Disconnected\" , it enters a \"FastBoot\" path that incorrectly routes USB lanes to a nonexistent DUT (much in the same way as an A-to-C cable would.) As an aside, it implicitly breaks uServo Type-A port functionality when Servo is \"unplugged from DUT\".\n\nWill submit a cleanup CL to try to address underlying concerns.\n\nWe may have to ensure all usb_mux drivers properly handle \"Disconnected\" state. This is actually /required/ per USB-IF compliance requirements: \"Type-C Functional MOI\" TD.4.1.1 and TD.4.11.1 which govern D+/D- isolation behavior.",
